{
  "about": "Money-safety contract shared by both libraries (Python ab0t-quota 0.7.3 / Go ab0t-quota-go v0.3.2). (1) `auth_delivered_event_types`: the only event types the ab0t auth service delivers to a webhook subscription (both auth engines) — a handler on any other type never runs from a real delivery. (2) `signup_gift_events`: the delivered types the default sign-up gift listens on, and therefore what `subscribe-events` subscribes to by default. `never_delivered_legacy_gift_events` are the names the Go library listened on before v0.3.2: still accepted by the receiver (replays, backfills and ledger rows written under them keep working) and never subscribed to by default. (3) `jwt_claim`: the default tier claim both libraries read, and the old Go default read as a fallback (only when jwt_claim_key is not set, only when the canonical claim is absent, only when its value names a tier in the config). (4) Startup texts both libraries print. (5) `price_list_403`: a 403 to the price-list publish means billing has not bound the service name to the calling account; it is retried rarely, capped, with these exact capability strings. (6) `money_doctor`: the `doctor --money` checks (same ids, names and grades in both libraries) and shared cases: a config plus the facts a doctor run gathered (null = not checked) -> the grade of every check. Byte-identical copy in ab0t-quota/tests/ and ab0t-quota-go/testdata/.",
  "auth_delivered_event_types": ["auth.agent.suspended", "auth.user.login", "auth.user.registered", "org.member.added", "org.member.removed"],
  "signup_gift_events": {
    "default": ["auth.user.registered"],
    "grant_on_member_joined": ["auth.user.registered", "org.member.added"]
  },
  "never_delivered_legacy_gift_events": ["org.created", "user.org_assigned"],
  "undelivered_subscription_warning_template": "auth does not deliver {event_types} to webhook subscriptions — a handler on it never runs from a real delivery (delivered: auth.agent.suspended, auth.user.login, auth.user.registered, org.member.added, org.member.removed)",
  "existing_subscription_missing_events_template": "auth-event subscription {id} exists but does not listen to {missing}: those events never reach this service, so the sign-up gift does not arrive for them. Auth cannot edit a subscription: {fix}",
